# Are there more mobile phone subscriptions than people on Earth?
subtitle: "Three claims about phones and the internet, true or myth, with two hosts arguing, then how rare a mobile was in 1990."
tags: ["computing","data","culture"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"More phones than people\" stamp \"TRUE OR MYTH?\""

## Are there more mobile phone subscriptions than people on Earth?
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - '1990'
      - '2025'
    values:
      - 0.2
      - 111
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 130
    y_label: Mobile subscriptions per 100 people
    bar_colors: same
    icons:
      - {of: telephone receiver, set: twemoji}
      - {of: mobile phone, set: twemoji}
    label_size: 40
sources:
    - id: owid_mob
      title: Mobile phone subscriptions per 100 people
      authors: Our World in Data, from the International Telecommunication Union (ITU) via the World Bank
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/mobile-cellular-subscriptions-per-100-people
      finding: 'world: 111.5 subscriptions per 100 people in 2025, 0.2 in 1990; low-income countries: 69 per 100 in 2025'
    - id: owid_net
      title: Share of the population using the Internet
      authors: Our World in Data, from the International Telecommunication Union (ITU) via the World Bank
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/share-of-individuals-using-the-internet
      finding: 'low-income countries: 23 % used the internet in 2025; world 74 %'

    icon i1 size 320 set twemoji x 320 y 380 icon_look picture of "mobile phone" hidden true
    text l1 "Claim 1 of 3" #2f2b26 x 320 y 195 font_size 54 hidden true
    icon i1b size 260 set twemoji x 700 y 380 icon_look picture of "people holding hands" hidden true
    text v1 "more phones than people?" #5e584e x 500 y 590 font_size 50 hidden true
    icon i2 size 320 set twemoji x 320 y 380 icon_look picture of coin hidden true
    text l2 "Claim 2 of 3" #2f2b26 x 320 y 195 font_size 54 hidden true
    text v2 "poorest countries: few phones?" #5e584e x 500 y 590 font_size 50 hidden true
    icon i3 size 320 set twemoji x 320 y 380 icon_look picture of "globe with meridians" hidden true
    text l3 "Claim 3 of 3" #2f2b26 x 320 y 195 font_size 54 hidden true
    text v3 "poorest countries: mostly online?" #5e584e x 500 y 590 font_size 50 hidden true
    text n1 "111 per 100" #2f6b8f cites ["owid_mob"] x 720 y 210 font_size 60 hidden true
    text n2 "69 per 100" #b5482e cites ["owid_mob"] x 720 y 380 font_size 72 hidden true
    text n3 "1 in 4" #b5482e cites ["owid_net"] x 720 y 380 font_size 80 hidden true
    text x500 "1 in 500" above bar_1 gap 40 #b5482e cites ["owid_mob"] font_size 56 hidden true

    card title "More phones than people?"

A: Are there more mobile phone subscriptions than people on Earth? That's the first of three claims.
    draw i1 i1b v1

B: Myth, surely. My grandmother doesn't have one.
    draw l1

    quiz "True or myth?"
        right: True. About a hundred and eleven for every hundred people, because many of us carry two SIMs, a work one and a private one.
        + True
        * Myth

    draw n1

    pause 0.8

    erase i1 i1b v1 l1 n1

A: Claim two: in the poorest countries, few people have a mobile subscription.
    draw i2 l2 v2

B: That one's true. No money, no phone.
    highlight i2

    quiz "True or myth?"
        right: Myth. Even in low-income countries there are about sixty-nine subscriptions for every hundred people.
        * True
        + Myth

    draw n2

    pause 0.8

    erase i2 l2 v2 n2

B: Sixty-nine! Then surely most people there are online, too. That's claim three.
    draw i3 l3 v3

    quiz "True or myth?"
        right: Myth. Only about one in four is online there. A phone that calls and texts is not a phone on the internet.
        * True
        + Myth

B: Two wrong out of three. I need a better phone.
    draw n3

    erase i3 l3 v3 n3

A: And look how fast it happened. Today, a hundred and eleven per hundred people.
    draw axes bar_2

B: And in 1990? That bar barely leaves the floor.
    draw bar_1 x500

A: About one in five hundred had one. From a rare brick to more phones than people, in thirty-five years.
    highlight bar_2

